Minimum Cost to Cut a Stick (Dynamic Programming)

This problem is frequently asked in top companies and GATE-level DP, but you haven’t listed it anywhere.

🧠 Problem Statement

You are given a wooden stick of length n.

You are also given an array cuts[], where each value represents a position where the stick must be cut.

🧾 Rule:

The cost of making a cut is equal to the current length of the stick being cut.

The order of cuts matters.

Your task is to find the minimum total cost to cut the stick at all given positions.

📘 Example
Input
n = 7
cuts = [1, 3, 4, 5]

Explanation (High level)

If you cut smartly, you minimize total cost.

✔ Best cutting order minimizes repeated large stick cuts.

Output
16

💡 Key Observation

Each cut splits the stick

Every future cut cost depends on the length of the current segment

This is a Range Dynamic Programming problem

🧩 Algorithm (Step-by-Step)

Add boundaries:

Insert 0 and n into the cuts list

Sort the cuts

Use DP[i][j]

Minimum cost to cut stick between cuts[i] and cuts[j]

Try all possible intermediate cuts k between i and j

Choose minimum:

dp[i][j] = min(
    cuts[j] - cuts[i] + dp[i][k] + dp[k][j]
)

⏱ Time & Space Complexity
Metric	Value
Time	O(n³)
Space	O(n²)
🧑‍💻 Java Code (Clean & Interview-Ready)
import java.util.*;

public class MinCostToCutStick {

    public static int minCost(int n, int[] cuts) {
        int m = cuts.length;

        // Step 1: Create new array with boundaries
        int[] newCuts = new int[m + 2];
        newCuts[0] = 0;
        newCuts[m + 1] = n;

        // Step 2: Copy cuts
        for (int i = 0; i < m; i++) {
            newCuts[i + 1] = cuts[i];
        }

        // Step 3: Sort cuts
        Arrays.sort(newCuts);

        // Step 4: DP table
        int[][] dp = new int[m + 2][m + 2];

        // Step 5: Fill DP
        for (int length = 2; length < m + 2; length++) {
            for (int i = 0; i + length < m + 2; i++) {
                int j = i + length;
                dp[i][j] = Integer.MAX_VALUE;

                for (int k = i + 1; k < j; k++) {
                    int cost = newCuts[j] - newCuts[i]
                             + dp[i][k]
                             + dp[k][j];
                    dp[i][j] = Math.min(dp[i][j], cost);
                }

                if (dp[i][j] == Integer.MAX_VALUE) {
                    dp[i][j] = 0;
                }
            }
        }

        return dp[0][m + 1];
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int n = 7;
        int[] cuts = {1, 3, 4, 5};

        System.out.println(minCost(n, cuts));
    }
}

